   "Bus wiring follows the image. SCL (A5) of both boards and one 4.7 k\u03a9 resistor meet in breadboard strip 10t. SDA (A4) of both boards and the other 4.7 k\u03a9 resistor meet in strip 12t. The other end of each resistor goes to the top 3V3 rail, which is fed by a red wire from the reader's 3V3 pin. The image draws these joins as crossing lines. It does not show a breadboard.",
   "The text says SDA is on A4 and SCL on A5. The image's teal line is A5 (SCL) and its yellow line is A4 (SDA), and both boards are wired the same way.",
   "The tutorial lists 2 mini breadboards but the circuit only needs one for the bus. bb2 is in the parts list but has no connections. The image does not show where it goes.",
   "The pull-up supply is the reader's 3V3 pin (3.3 V), which suits the 3.3 V logic of the Nano 33 IoT. GND is joined between the boards with the brown wire. USB cables power each board from the computer and carry serial.",
   "The USB cable has no ports in the catalogue, so the USB edges use a null port on the cable side and the board's USB port."
